{"id": "EUVD-2026-107001", "enisaUuid": "975b77c9-65f9-36eb-914f-41a192c4cc8b", "description": "vLLM before 0.31.0 uses a client-supplied multimodal uuid verbatim as cache identity with no consistency check on cache hits, allowing engine crashes. Unauthenticated attackers can desynchronize the P0/P1 processor caches to trigger a fatal token-placeholder mismatch, killing the entire serving instance until restarted.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T00:36:27", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T15:50:53", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/security/advisories/GHSA-p92p-rxj5-7p2x", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/vllm-before-0.31.0-remote-engine-crash-via-forged-multimodal-uuid"], "aliases": ["GHSA-hfwf-hgvp-4rr8", "CVE-2026-114050"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "7d171aab-8fb9-3da8-a18c-bcf33ec4d5a2", "product": {"name": "vllm", "vendor": {"name": "vllm-project"}}, "product_version": "0 <0.31.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6d23dafc-3082-339b-b245-00c08023dcd9", "vendor": {"name": "vllm-project"}}], "isExploited": false}